silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_03_cite_as_kleisli_arrow_concrete_anchor_4#mittensasterminusofcitechain a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.01_orientation.chapters.14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline.sections.03_cite_as_kleisli_arrow.concrete_anchor_4#mittensasterminusofcitechain" .
silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_03_cite_as_kleisli_arrow_concrete_anchor_4#mittensasterminusofcitechain silm:hasLongDescription "The MittensAsTerminusOfCiteChain is Mittens appears at the right of the cite-kleisli demonstration chain to anchor the claim that cite (which models the unit eta of the free monad) is the first Kleisli arrow of the multi-step path that ends at the colimit apex. Mittens is the concrete cat (Mrs Hendersons silver-furred domestic cat, vet record 77, microchip 2018, body mass 4.1kg). The diagram visibly carries the eta-wrap step at its source and the glue commitment at its target, so the role of cite as eta_Witness is inspectable end-to-end." .
